# Database & Prisma

Canonical: [Database guidelines](mdc:docs/database/DATABASE_GUIDELINES.md).

## Server-only

Every file in `src/server/**` begins with
`import "server-only";`. No React component or client hook may import
anything from `src/server/**`, `@prisma/client`, or
`src/lib/env/server`.

## Access rules

- `getPrisma()` from
  [`src/server/db/prisma.ts`](mdc:src/server/db/prisma.ts) is the only
  way to obtain a Prisma Client.
- Put queries in a repository under
  [`src/server/repositories/`](mdc:src/server/repositories/). One
  repository per aggregate, not per table.
- Repositories return DTOs, not raw Prisma records. Services compose
  repositories and enforce invariants.
- Never return sensitive fields (hashes, tokens, PII) to callers that
  surface to the client.

## Transactions

Use `prisma.$transaction` for multi-write operations that must succeed
or fail atomically. Prefer the interactive callback form when a middle
step depends on earlier results.

## Migrations

- Local: `npm run prisma:migrate -- --name <descriptive>`.
- Production: `npm run prisma:deploy` only.
- **Never** `prisma migrate dev`, `prisma db push`, or any destructive
  statement against production without explicit authorisation and a
  verified backup.

## Raw SQL

Allowed only via Prisma's tagged templates
(`prisma.$queryRaw` with `${param}`). Never concatenate user input into
SQL strings.

## Schema

Edit [`prisma/schema.prisma`](mdc:prisma/schema.prisma) following the
conventions in
[DATABASE_GUIDELINES](mdc:docs/database/DATABASE_GUIDELINES.md).
After editing, run `npm run db:validate` and `npm run prisma:generate`.

